PR #1 — Repository foundation, engineering standards and delivery plan
Branch: chore/repo-foundation          Depends on: —                Status: DONE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  The rulebook and the plan, before any application code exists. Nothing here
  ships to users; everything here decides whether the next 29 PRs stay clean.

IMPLEMENTS
  [ ] tasks.todo (this file) as the single source of delivery truth
  [ ] README.md — what the product is, the non-negotiables, how to run it
  [ ] CONTRIBUTING.md — the global rules above, expanded with examples
  [ ] CLAUDE.md — agent protocol: read tasks.todo first, one PR per task
  [ ] .github/pull_request_template.md with the Definition of Done checklist
      and a mandatory SEO section
  [ ] .github/workflows/ci.yml — typecheck, lint, unit+coverage gate, build,
      storybook build, test-runner screenshots, Playwright, Lighthouse CI
  [ ] .github/CODEOWNERS, .editorconfig, .gitignore, .nvmrc (pin Node 22)
  [ ] LICENSE, SECURITY.md (biometric-data posture stated explicitly)
  [ ] Branch protection notes: require CI green, require 1 review, linear history

EDGE CASES
  [ ] CI must fail — not warn — when coverage drops below 100%
  [ ] Concurrency group cancels superseded runs so stale jobs don't block merges
  [ ] Workflow permissions set to read-only by default, elevated per-job
  [ ] Node version pinned identically in .nvmrc, CI matrix and package.json
  [ ] Playwright browsers cached in CI or every run pays the download
  [ ] Storybook build must not be allowed to pass with a11y violations
  [ ] Dependabot/Renovate configured but grouped, so it can't flood the queue

SEO
  n/a — but the PR template's SEO checklist created here gates every later PR.

TESTS
  CI self-test: a deliberately failing fixture proves the coverage gate bites.

