  [x] Mobile menu is a native <details>, so every link is in the static HTML
      whether open or closed. Asserted in a unit test AND by fetching the
      served HTML in Playwright, which is what a crawler actually receives.
  [x] Theme toggle: no flash (ColorSchemeScript runs pre-paint), no hydration
      mismatch
  [x] Breadcrumb structured data is built from the same array as the visible
      trail, so the two cannot diverge
  [x] Footer features a curated subset, not the registry. 100+ links on every
      page dilutes what each passes and weighs down every route.
  [x] Native disclosure means no keyboard trap to build or get wrong
  [x] MOBILE OVERFLOW — caught by the screenshot suite, not by review. At 390px
      the brand plus menu plus a three-option theme control did not fit and the
      toggle ran off-screen. Fixed by moving the theme control into the
      disclosure panel on narrow screens; only one instance is ever displayed.
  [ ] Suspense fallbacks per segment — deferred until a segment actually
      suspends, which is the analysis work

SEO
  [ ] Every nav item a real <a href>; verify by parsing static HTML in CI
  [ ] 404 returns a genuine 404 status, not a soft 200

TESTS
  Unit + axe. Stories for open/closed menu, both themes. Playwright: keyboard
  navigation, skip link, 404 status code.


