PR #15 — Worker infrastructure, typed protocol and the fake-model test layer
Branch: feat/worker-infrastructure     Depends on: #14                Status: DONE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  The Web Worker plus its typed request/response protocol — and the fixture
  layer that lets every later PR reach 100% coverage without loading 5MB of
  WASM in a unit test. This is the mocking story for this product.

IMPLEMENTS
  [x] Worker entry point, bootstrap and a browser worker factory that
      feature-detects rather than assuming Worker exists
  [x] Discriminated-union message protocol, correlation IDs, typed both ways
  [x] Progress reporting, cancellation, timeout
  [x] Structured error propagation across the boundary — structured clone drops
      the prototype and stack, so errors are serialised to a branchable code
  [x] Detector interface so the real MediaPipe backend and a deterministic fake
      backend are interchangeable. createDetector() is the single seam PR #17
      replaces; until then it reports detector-unavailable rather than throwing
      at module load, which would misreport every request as worker-crashed
  [x] Fake detector deriving landmarks from each fixture's generation spec, so
      ground truth is exact by construction rather than measured
  [x] Fake worker running the real handler in memory, with failToStart,
      crashOnNextMessage and neverRespond to reach the failure paths
  [ ] DEFERRED to #16 — OffscreenCanvas bootstrap. It belongs with image
      ingestion, where there is something to decode and draw; adding it here
      would be untestable scaffolding with no caller.
  [ ] DEFERRED to #26 — Storybook decorator injecting the fake backend. There
      is no analysis UI to decorate yet. The Vitest side needs no setup: the
      fake is injected through createWorker, by construction.

EDGE CASES
  [x] Worker fails to start (CSP, blocked, private mode) => typed
      worker-unavailable, not a raw TypeError
  [x] Worker crashes mid-task => in-flight requests fail, listeners detached,
      the instance dropped, and the next call builds a fresh one
  [x] Cancellation arrives after completion => must not resolve twice. Every
      pending request settles exactly once, whatever path reaches it
  [x] Two analyses in flight; the stale one must be discarded, not rendered
  [x] A worker-reported cancellation settles the promise rather than leaving
      the caller waiting out the timeout
  [x] A cancellation mid-analysis stops the work at the next checkpoint rather
      than being noticed only at the end — on a phone that is seconds of
      blocked work for a screen the user has already left
  [ ] DEFERRED to #16 — out-of-memory on large images, structured-clone
      failures, and detached ArrayBuffers after transfer. All three are
      properties of the payload, and there is no image decoding yet to produce
      one. The error codes (out-of-memory) are already in the protocol.
  [ ] DEFERRED to #16 — Safari OffscreenCanvas feature detection, with the
      OffscreenCanvas work itself.

SEO
  [x] Worker created lazily on first use, never at module load, and referenced
      through new URL() so the bundler emits it as its own chunk — zero bytes
      on first paint

TESTS
  Unit: protocol, correlation, cancellation, timeout, crash recovery, the fake
  detector's own fidelity, and the fake worker's own contract. 100% coverage.
  [ ] DEFERRED to #26 — real worker round-trip in Playwright. It needs a page
      that runs an analysis, and the first one lands with the checker UI.

NOTE
  This PR also fixes CI, which had been red on every run since PR #2 and was
  never checked. The build refuses to start without an origin — deliberately,
  since a missing one produces relative canonicals and de-indexes the site —
  and the workflow supplied none, so every job after the build was skipped.
  Local builds passed only because .env.local is present and gitignored.

