  [ ] NO ADS ON THE CHECKER PAGE. Not a preference — a hard constraint.
      We invite people to open DevTools and watch the Network tab to verify
      their photo is never uploaded. An ad stack fires dozens of requests to
      unknown third parties, so a visitor doing exactly the verification we
      asked for sees a wall of traffic. That destroys the strongest claim we
      have, on the page where it matters most. Ads live on requirements, FAQ
      and guide pages; the checker stays clean, and its emptiness is part of
      the pitch.
  [ ] AdSense rejects thin tool pages — confirm every route has real content
  [ ] Re-run Lighthouse after ads; budgets still apply
  [ ] Ad-carrying pages are the informational ones, which are also the ones AI
      Overviews are eating. Do not plan the business around display alone.
TESTS  Lighthouse with ads enabled; CLS assertion on ad-bearing routes.


